This document provides reference architectures and design decisions for applications and services hosted on IBM Power Virtual Server to integrate with IBM managed watsonx SaaS services or client managed watsonx software in IBM Cloud.
{: shortdesc}

## Overview
{: #overview}

This article discusses how to integrate Power Virtual Server and watsonx, and take advantages of both of them. The diagram below highlights the high-level communication between Power Virtual Server and watsonx services:

1. To extend the mission critical workloads with watsonx, the applications hosted on Power Virtual Server can invoke inference APIs on watsonx service endpoint;
2. To allow cloud native AI applications or watsonx services to make use of the data or applications hosted on Power Virtual Server, watsonx needs to access the private services hosted on Power Virtual Server. The watsonx.governance service can also use similar path to monitor AI models hosted on Power Virtual Server if needed.

![Power Virtual Server and watsonx high-level communication](../images/overview-high-level.svg){: caption="Power Virtual Server and watsonx high-level communication" caption-side="bottom"}

### IBM Power Virtual Server and watsonx SaaS integration
{: #architecture-diagram-saas}

First, let's discuss Power Virtual Server and watsonx SaaS integration. Let's take a look at two flavors of the reference architecture.

In this case, client has some workloads on Power Virtual Server, which could be databases, applications, or even AI models hosted on Power Virtual Server. If the client also has other cloud workloads in VPC, we would recommend multiple VPCs for separation of concerns between edge networking controls, provider management, and consumer workloads. Refer to [VPC reference architecture](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/framework-financial-services?topic=framework-financial-services-vpc-architecture-about&format=markdown) in IBM Cloud Framework for Financial Services for recommended architecture and best practices.

![Power Virtual Server and watsonx SaaS integration (with workloads in VPC and on Power Virtual Server)](../images/powervs-ai-SaaS.svg "Power Virtual Server and watsonx SaaS integration (with workloads in VPC and on Power Virtual Server)"){: caption="Power Virtual Server and watsonx SaaS integration (with workloads in VPC and on Power Virtual Server)" caption-side="bottom"}

IBM Power Virtual Server and watsonx SaaS connectivity:

![Power Virtual Server and watsonx SaaS integration (with workloads on Power Virtual Server)](../images/powervs-ai-SaaS-edge.svg "Power Virtual Server and watsonx SaaS integration (with workloads on Power Virtual Server)"){: caption="Power Virtual Server and watsonx SaaS integration (with workloads on Power Virtual Server)" caption-side="bottom"}

IBM provides different flavors of deployable architectures to automatically provision Power Virtual Server environment. Refer to [Power Systems Virtual Server with VPC landing zone](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/powervs-vpc?topic=powervs-vpc-automation-solution-overview&format=markdown) for details.

